        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Describe revoked Ollama API keys accurately",
        "body": "## Summary\n- describe rejected Ollama keys as invalid or revoked\n- remove the inaccurate claim that Ollama API keys expire\n- document the provider key lifecycle\n\n## Live proof\nThe `OllamaUsageFetcherTests` explicitly verifies the localized string describing revocation:\n```text\nswift test --disable-sandbox --filter OllamaUsageFetcherTests\n...\n✔ Test \"api authorization error describes revocation\" passed after 0.001 seconds.\n✔ Suite OllamaUsageFetcherTests passed after 0.002 seconds.\n✔ Test run with 19 tests in 1 suite passed after 0.002 seconds.\n```\n\n## Provider proof\nOllama official authentication documentation states that API keys do not currently expire and can be revoked at any time:\nhttps://docs.ollama.com/api/authentication\n\nThe old `invalid or expired` message contradicted the provider contract; `invalid or revoked` matches it. No credentials or Keychain access were required.\n\n## Tests\n- `swift test --disable-sandbox --filter OllamaUsageFetcherTests` (19 passed)\n- changed Swift files pass SwiftFormat and SwiftLint strict\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD`\n\n## Commits\n- exactly 3: implementation, tests, documentation",
